  "interpretation": {
    "june": "A page displaying June 6, captured June 13, explicitly identifies all four pilot awards and a fifth VISN 20 order. VISN 8 excluding Puerto Rico maps directly to 36C10X24N0089. The four pilot base periods run June 1, 2024 through May 31, 2025. They are not original-action or filing dates. The June service-area labels plus the separately reviewed GAO footnotes support sixteen provisional pairs across thirteen dockets; the shared supplemental docket is not an independent event for each award.",
    "september": "The page displaying September 4, captured September 6, lists nineteen service areas, fourteen marked TBD. VISN 23 is absent from this display, not proven unawarded. It repeats 36C10X24N0074 for VISN 19 and VISN 22, conflicting with June's VISN 22 order 36C10X24N0108. VISN 20's displayed start changes from May 10 to June 1; its end remains May 9, 2025. Do not correct these cells or interpret display changes as contract modifications.",
    "stay": "Four displayed area rows carry the star note, but only three distinct parent/child keys do because of the repeated VISN 22 key. The note reports a current GAO protest and stay of performance, without start, end, original stay document or case IDs. Preserve it as an archived agency statement at this snapshot, not an exact stay interval, a finding of capture or a blanket four-award timing clearance.",
    "remaining": "Original solicitations and record-specific offer-count provenance remain missing. The later VISN 22 conflict requires independent source review. All baseline award filedDate and docket piid cells remain unchanged. Representative SAM coverage and historical exclusion intervals are not supplied by these archives."
  },
